  {
   "path": "sections.story.4.zh",
   "before": "达尔文收到论文后的做法，莱尔和胡克写得很具体：他写信给莱尔，提议征得华莱士本人同意后，尽快把这篇论文发表。两位中间人表示赞成，但附了一个条件：达尔文不能像他（为照顾华莱士）“强烈倾向”的那样，扣下自己关于同一主题的手稿。信里记下的是达尔文的倾向：把发表的机会让给对方。",
   "after": "达尔文收到论文后的做法，莱尔和胡克写得很具体：他写信给莱尔，提议征得华莱士本人同意后，尽快把这篇论文发表。两位中间人表示赞成，但附了一个条件：达尔文不能像信中所说他（为照顾华莱士）强烈倾向于做的那样，扣下自己关于同一主题的手稿。信里记下的是达尔文的倾向：把发表的机会让给对方。",
   "issues": [
    "F2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "path": "sections.analysis.1.zh",
   "before": "作者把他们的做法概括为：算，但要公开兑现。作者列出的替代做法至少有三种，各有代价：由达尔文先单独发表；只发华莱士，把达尔文的优先权留给他日后自述；或者都等达尔文的完整著作出来再说。其中第二种与信中所记达尔文的倾向相对应：他提议尽快发表华莱士的论文，并强烈倾向于扣下自己的手稿；其余两种是作者提出的对照选项，不是材料里的记载。实际被选中的是第四条：三份材料同场宣读，日期写进正文，理由写给一位秘书并公开发表。莱尔和胡克自己说，这样做的依据是让经年思考、建立在大量事实上的观点立刻成为别人可以出发的目标。分配交给了程序，当事人让步的意愿只是其中一步。",
   "after": "作者把他们的做法概括为：算，但要公开兑现。作者列出的替代做法至少有三种，各有代价：由达尔文先单独发表；只发华莱士，把达尔文的优先权留给他日后自述；或者都等达尔文的完整著作出来再说。其中第二种的前半（只发华莱士）与信中所记达尔文的倾向相对应：他提议征得华莱士同意后尽快发表其论文，并强烈倾向于扣下自己的手稿；“把达尔文的优先权留给他日后自述”这半句，与其余两种一样，是作者提出的对照选项，不是材料里的记载。实际被选中的是第四条：三份材料同场宣读，日期写进正文，理由写给一位秘书并公开发表。莱尔和胡克自己说，这样做的依据是让经年思考、建立在大量事实上的观点立刻成为别人可以出发的目标。分配交给了程序，当事人让步的意愿只是其中一步。",
   "issues": [
    "F3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "path": "sections.analysis.1.en",
   "before": "The author's summary of their course is: yes, but it has to be cashed in publicly. The author sets out at least three alternative courses, each with its own price: Darwin publishing alone first; only Wallace published, with Darwin left to state his own priority later; or everyone waiting for Darwin's complete book. The second corresponds to the inclination the letter records in Darwin: he proposed that Wallace's essay be published as soon as possible, and was strongly inclined to withhold his own memoir; the other two are options constructed by the author for contrast, not episodes recorded in the documents. The course actually taken was a fourth: three sets of material read together in one session, the dates printed in the body of the text, the reasoning addressed to a secretary and made public. The warrant Lyell and Hooker gave was that views founded on a wide deduction from facts and matured by years of reflection should at once become a goal from which others might start. The allocation was handed to a procedure; a party's willingness to give way was one step in it.",
   "after": "The author's summary of their course is: yes, but it has to be cashed in publicly. The author sets out at least three alternative courses, each with its own price: Darwin publishing alone first; only Wallace published, with Darwin left to state his own priority later; or everyone waiting for Darwin's complete book. The first half of the second (publishing only Wallace) corresponds to the inclination the letter records in Darwin: he proposed to obtain Wallace's consent and have Wallace's essay published as soon as possible, and was strongly inclined to withhold his own memoir; the part about Darwin stating his own priority later, like the other two options, was constructed by the author for contrast and is not recorded in the documents. The course actually taken was a fourth: three sets of material read together in one session, the dates printed in the body of the text, the reasoning addressed to a secretary and made public. The warrant Lyell and Hooker gave was that views founded on a wide deduction from facts and matured by years of reflection should at once become a goal from which others might start. The allocation was handed to a procedure; a party's willingness to give way was one step in it.",
   "issues": [
    "F3"
   ]
  }
 ],
